                  {
                    "value": "2 \u00b7 Cost of Debt & the Tax Shield \u2014 from scratch",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "13pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "A lender starts from the same floor, rf, and adds a markup for the chance of not being repaid \u2014 the credit spread. Kd = rf + spread = 4.53 + 2.00 = 6.53%.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Now the tax twist: the state taxes profit AFTER interest, so every $1 of interest shrinks taxable profit by $1 and saves tax \u00d7 $1 = $0.25. The firm's true cost is what is left: Kd \u00d7 (1 \u2212 tax) = 6.53 \u00d7 0.75 = 4.90%.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Book cross-check from the statements themselves: interest expense \u00f7 total debt = 25.4 \u00f7 366.0 = 6.94% \u2014 close to the market build, as it should be.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "\u2192 tab 3 and tab 8 \u00b7 Calc Build-Out",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
